summary:
  The larger view fills its room whatever the picture's own size.

history:
  A station's logo of 32 pixels, clicked larger, was drawn 600 wide. Of
  51 logos cached on one desk 12 are 32 pixels or less. The larger view
  stops at twice a picture's own pixels. This mutant takes the limit out.

target:
  package/contents/ui/CoverLogic.js

find:
      return Math.min(roomW / natW, roomH / natH, STRETCH / (_side(ratio) || 1));

replace:
      return Math.min(roomW / natW, roomH / natH);

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_coverlogic.qml::test_the_larger_picture_is_whole_and_at_most_twice_its_pixels.
  Line-neutral.
